From 7c3f1a9e2b4d5c6a8f0e1d2c3b4a5f6e7d8c9b0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yanan.he <yanan.he@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Thu, 06 Aug 2026 00:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] utilities: build comp_err when cross compiling with emulator

comp_err is wrapped in IF(NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING): upstream expects a
host-installed comp_err to be found in PATH during cross builds. The
ADD_CUSTOM_COMMAND that generates mysqld_error.h/ername.h/errmsg.h/
errmsg.sys references plain "comp_err", which on a cross build without
the target resolves to a bare PATH lookup and fails:

  cd .../build/utilities && comp_err --charset=... && cd ...
  /bin/sh: 1: comp_err: not found

When CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR is set, build comp_err as a normal
target binary instead. The custom command references the target name,
so CMake substitutes the full path and prepends the emulator
automatically (same-directory target), and adds the target-level
dependency. Cross builds without an emulator keep upstream semantics
(host tool from PATH).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [cross compilation specific]

Signed-off-by: yanan.he <yanan.he@linux.alibaba.com>
---
 utilities/CMakeLists.txt | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/utilities/CMakeLists.txt b/utilities/CMakeLists.txt
index 83a8b6a..f2e1c9d 100644
--- a/utilities/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/utilities/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -30,7 +30,12 @@ IF(NOT WITH_DEBUG)
   DISABLE_DOCUMENTATION_WARNINGS()
 ENDIF()
 
-IF(NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
+# Cross build with an emulator (CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR): comp_err
+# is still needed at build time to generate mysqld_error.h & friends.
+# Build it as a target binary; the ADD_CUSTOM_COMMAND below references
+# the target name, so CMake substitutes the path and prepends the
+# emulator automatically.
+IF(NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING OR CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR)
   MYSQL_ADD_EXECUTABLE(comp_err
     comp_err.cc
     COMPONENT Test
